Your function must not use array indexing (you cannot use square brackets `[]` in your answer), and it must not call another function. It should use a pointer (or pointers), pointer dereferencing, and pointer arithmetic instead of array indexing. Note that `ptr2lastmin` does not receive the length of the array as input.

questions.answer:
```c
int *ptr2lastmin(const int *a) {
    const int *min = a;                    // pointer to the smallest so far
    for (const int *p = a + 1; *p != 0; p++) {
        if (*p <= *min) {                  // <= so a later tie wins
            min = p;
        }
    }
    return (int *) min;
}
```

